WEBVTT

00:06.832 --> 00:07.981
Oww...

00:07.981 --> 00:08.081
Oww...

00:08.083 --> 00:10.856
Who the heck drinks orange juice
with their mouth cut?

00:10.858 --> 00:13.467
Shut up! Vitamin C's supposed
to help with cuts!

00:13.469 --> 00:15.134
Don't you mean dry skin?

00:15.375 --> 00:17.281
Protein's what you're looking for!

00:17.283 --> 00:18.265
Thanks for the food!

00:18.267 --> 00:20.570
That was my last one, you jerk!

00:20.570 --> 00:20.596
I'm gonna rub this lemon
all over your wounds!
That was my last one, you jerk!

00:20.596 --> 00:21.503
I'm gonna rub this lemon
all over your wounds!

00:21.503 --> 00:23.440
Everyone's lively as always.
I'm gonna rub this lemon
all over your wounds!

00:23.440 --> 00:23.830
Everyone's lively as always.

00:23.832 --> 00:24.598
Yeah.

00:24.944 --> 00:27.641
I'm glad Anzai-san's feeling better too.

00:27.643 --> 00:29.054
Oh, right! Nirei!

00:29.356 --> 00:31.191
Any word from Sakura?

00:31.193 --> 00:34.552
No, he hasn't read my messages either.

00:36.688 --> 00:39.864
I wonder what's going on
with Sakura-kun today.

00:39.866 --> 00:41.904
Maybe he overslept?

00:41.906 --> 00:45.330
At this hour?
It's almost past lunch, you know?

00:45.632 --> 00:49.189
He seemed pretty down after the fight...

00:49.191 --> 00:50.704
I'm kinda worried.

00:51.185 --> 00:52.979
Let's try calling him.

00:56.004 --> 00:58.285
Ah, hello? Sakura-san?

00:58.287 --> 01:00.207
Thank goodness. You alright?

01:00.507 --> 01:02.730
Huh?! Sakura-san? Saku—

01:04.704 --> 01:06.219
He hung up on me.

01:06.221 --> 01:08.410
Wait, is he okay?

01:08.412 --> 01:09.894
I'm just guessing, but...

01:10.328 --> 01:13.104
I think Sakura-san caught a cold.

01:13.413 --> 01:15.329
He sounded pretty sick.

01:16.548 --> 01:18.985
-What?!-

02:50.278 --> 02:52.826
Don't you think we bought a bit too much?

02:53.298 --> 02:55.748
Everyone's worried about Sakura-kun.

02:55.750 --> 02:58.489
We were all practically ready
to visit him together.

02:58.491 --> 02:59.998
Right.

03:00.395 --> 03:01.601
Still,

03:01.603 --> 03:04.386
I didn't expect Sakura-san's house
to be this close.

03:04.864 --> 03:08.570
He said he was from out of town,
so I assumed he lived far away.

03:09.036 --> 03:12.897
Maybe he enrolled here because his family
had to relocate for work?

03:12.899 --> 03:13.687
Well,

03:14.087 --> 03:15.762
we'll know once we get there.

03:18.044 --> 03:20.712
Ah, this is it. We're here...

03:20.944 --> 03:21.944
(OPEN FOR RENT)

03:26.521 --> 03:28.318
Oh, a haunted house!

03:28.320 --> 03:29.831
Hey, Suo-san!

03:30.081 --> 03:33.651
Wait, this place looks like
it's for singles.

03:33.653 --> 03:37.124
Y-Yeah, I wonder why.

03:41.652 --> 03:42.802
It's broken.

03:44.843 --> 03:45.690
It's not locked.

03:45.692 --> 03:47.880
H-Hey, we can't just barge in!

03:50.093 --> 03:52.033
Those are Sakura-kun's shoes.

03:52.881 --> 03:55.026
Sakura-kun! Hello!

04:00.704 --> 04:01.532
Uh...

04:01.534 --> 04:04.566
A-Are you sure he lives here?

04:04.568 --> 04:06.071
Pardon the intrusion!

04:06.073 --> 04:08.721
W-We really shouldn't be
barging in like this—

04:08.723 --> 04:09.701
Nire-kun.

04:09.906 --> 04:12.849
From the looks of it,
Sakura-kun's alone right now.

04:13.906 --> 04:16.506
What's worse, he's sick and can't move.

04:17.610 --> 04:20.710
What if something were to happen?

04:20.716 --> 04:22.600
S-Something...?

04:23.889 --> 04:26.830
H-He's gonna die alone!

04:26.830 --> 04:27.014
(KYAAAH!)
H-He's gonna die alone!

04:27.014 --> 04:28.000
(KYAAAH!)

04:28.229 --> 04:29.657
Shaddap!

04:29.659 --> 04:31.753
Who said you could barge in
and start yellin'?!

04:35.574 --> 04:37.346
You guys...

04:38.319 --> 04:39.937
S-Sakura-san!

04:40.295 --> 04:41.405
Why...

04:41.711 --> 04:42.896
...are you guys...

04:42.898 --> 04:45.213
W-We came to visit you!

04:45.215 --> 04:46.982
You seem really sick.

04:49.244 --> 04:50.745
Sorry for waking you up.

04:50.747 --> 04:52.682
Okay, let's get you back to bed.

04:52.684 --> 04:55.145
-Stop pushing me...
-Nire-kun, can you bring in the gifts?

04:55.657 --> 04:56.702
Sure!

05:04.173 --> 05:07.806
Sakura-kun, are you really living alone?

05:08.047 --> 05:09.698
Got a problem with that?

05:09.700 --> 05:11.229
Do you have any cold meds?

05:11.231 --> 05:12.303
Should we get you some?

05:12.305 --> 05:13.486
Nah...

05:13.488 --> 05:15.799
Then how about something to eat?

05:15.801 --> 05:17.315
I don't wanna eat...

05:18.314 --> 05:22.534
To think a big eater like you
would have no appetite...

05:23.668 --> 05:25.456
You're not even talking back.

05:27.296 --> 05:31.824
Still, I can't believe he's living alone
in a place like this.

05:32.395 --> 05:35.118
What happened to you, Sakura-san?

05:35.120 --> 05:36.120
Nire-kun.

05:37.140 --> 05:38.968
Can you hand that to Sakura-kun?

05:38.970 --> 05:41.332
Oh, right.

05:42.134 --> 05:44.457
Here, this is from everyone in class.

05:45.200 --> 05:49.049
We were all really worried about you,
so we got you some get-well gifts.

05:50.154 --> 05:52.266
I don't know your situation,

05:52.574 --> 05:54.627
but you're living alone,

05:55.505 --> 05:58.028
so please rely on us more.

05:58.991 --> 06:01.912
Right, I've been saying that
since yesterday.

06:02.190 --> 06:03.481
It's fine...

06:04.277 --> 06:08.006
I've always managed stuff like this
on my own.

06:08.599 --> 06:10.237
I'll just sleep it off...

06:10.824 --> 06:12.237
Nothin' to worry about.

06:14.902 --> 06:16.202
Y-You mean—

06:16.204 --> 06:17.204
Nire-kun.

06:17.449 --> 06:20.666
We already dropped the get-well gifts,
so let's not bother him for too long.

06:21.059 --> 06:22.059
Let's go.

06:22.061 --> 06:23.956
B-But...

06:24.409 --> 06:26.202
Let's just head back for today.

06:27.496 --> 06:29.468
O-Okay...

06:30.568 --> 06:31.943
Well then, Sakura-kun.

06:31.945 --> 06:32.884
Take care.

06:33.155 --> 06:35.390
Just contact us if you need anything.

06:43.462 --> 06:44.702
S-Suo-san!

06:44.704 --> 06:46.247
W-Wait up!

06:46.249 --> 06:47.643
Why are we heading back?

06:47.906 --> 06:49.675
Aren't you worried about him?

06:50.985 --> 06:52.105
It's not that.

06:54.256 --> 06:56.781
I don't know what happened to him,

06:57.302 --> 07:00.102
but from how that room looks
and how Sakura-kun's doing,

07:00.104 --> 07:02.540
he probably was living alone
for a long time.

07:02.542 --> 07:04.185
Then all the more reason to...

07:04.187 --> 07:08.034
Let's say you're lost,
and you're allowed to be given one thing.

07:08.036 --> 07:09.084
What would you pick?

07:09.086 --> 07:09.962
Huh?

07:12.668 --> 07:14.750
M-My phone.

07:14.752 --> 07:17.202
I can use it to look up my location.

07:17.452 --> 07:18.340
Right.

07:18.576 --> 07:22.141
That's because you know how
to use your phone, right?

07:23.089 --> 07:24.089
Yeah.

07:24.413 --> 07:27.881
When you're in trouble, and you're given
something you don't know how to use,

07:27.883 --> 07:29.781
it'll only make things worse, right?

07:30.438 --> 07:34.752
In Sakura-kun's case, it's like
he doesn't even know smartphones exist,

07:34.754 --> 07:36.281
let alone how to use one.

07:36.980 --> 07:37.163
(Junpei Kurita:
Yo, Sakura! How're you feeling?)

07:37.163 --> 07:38.980
I think that's what
friends are like to him.
(Junpei Kurita:
Yo, Sakura! How're you feeling?)

07:38.980 --> 07:39.980
(Yuri Kakiuchi:
Sent a stamp — ARE YOU OKAY?)
I think that's what
friends are like to him.

07:39.980 --> 07:40.815
(Masaki Anzai:
Be sure to rest up, alright?)
I think that's what
friends are like to him.

07:40.815 --> 07:41.360
(Masaki Anzai:
Be sure to rest up, alright?)

07:41.688 --> 07:44.680
That's why I figured we should
interact with him like we always do,

07:44.682 --> 07:47.330
so he won't tire himself out
physically or mentally.

07:48.560 --> 07:52.132
If he doesn't show up at school tomorrow,
let's visit him again.

07:52.385 --> 07:53.118
Okay?

07:57.044 --> 07:59.775
I get what you're trying to say...

08:00.909 --> 08:02.764
Even so, I...

08:02.769 --> 08:06.791
I want him to know he has friends,

08:07.828 --> 08:10.351
that he can rely on us
and leave things to us,

08:10.760 --> 08:13.519
that we can help him when he's in trouble.

08:15.408 --> 08:20.901
I promised Sakura-san that I'd show him
the way until he reached the top.

08:21.544 --> 08:25.663
Sakura-san's always
carving his own path forward.

08:25.997 --> 08:27.157
That's why,

08:27.159 --> 08:30.038
I want to at least be there for him
when he's in trouble.

08:30.597 --> 08:33.085
I just want to be of some help!

08:36.213 --> 08:37.041
Oh?

08:37.229 --> 08:38.782
Nire and Suo!

08:52.866 --> 08:55.110
(Get well soon~ - Kiryu)

08:55.112 --> 08:57.113
(Some Vitamin C for your cold! - Anzai)
(This is pretty good! - Kakiuchi)

08:57.114 --> 08:59.356
(Stay Hydrated! - Takanashi)
(Take care!! - Kurita)

09:02.011 --> 09:04.720
I've always managed on my own.

09:05.973 --> 09:08.133
I've always made it work by myself.

09:09.423 --> 09:13.142
That was... how it was supposed to be...

09:13.780 --> 09:16.157
The reason you couldn't move properly

09:16.159 --> 09:18.674
was because you saw your friends
getting hurt, don't you think?

09:19.875 --> 09:23.205
It's because you like them.

09:23.707 --> 09:24.912
Cut the crap.

09:25.050 --> 09:25.289
(Get well soon~) (Stay Hydrated!)
(Some Vitamin C for your cold!)

09:25.289 --> 09:27.550
How can liking or hating someone
make you freeze up?
(Get well soon~) (Stay Hydrated!)
(Some Vitamin C for your cold!)

09:27.550 --> 09:29.636
How can liking or hating someone
make you freeze up?

09:32.369 --> 09:33.484
What the hell?

09:34.363 --> 09:35.788
What the hell's wrong with me?

09:43.422 --> 09:44.944
W-Wait!

09:48.380 --> 09:49.556
Oh, sorry.

09:49.558 --> 09:50.653
Did I wake you up?

09:54.100 --> 09:55.540
Here you go.

09:55.803 --> 09:57.137
Egg congee.

09:57.139 --> 09:58.940
Just eat what you can.

10:03.843 --> 10:06.293
Hey, don't just gulp it down!

10:07.228 --> 10:10.559
Anyway, so you live alone?

10:10.891 --> 10:13.737
I wouldn't have guessed anyone lived here.

10:14.147 --> 10:16.031
At least put on some curtains?

10:16.530 --> 10:18.981
And don't you have way too little stuff?

10:18.983 --> 10:20.565
Are you a minimalist or something?

10:20.567 --> 10:22.065
Sh-Shut it!

10:22.067 --> 10:25.365
Well, I'm relieved you've got an appetite.

10:25.778 --> 10:28.493
I bumped into Nire and Suo earlier.

10:28.495 --> 10:30.821
Nire was really panicking.

10:31.317 --> 10:34.054
Sheesh, that was completely unnecessary.

10:34.360 --> 10:34.440
(SLAP)

10:34.440 --> 10:35.550
Unnecessary?!
(SLAP)

10:35.550 --> 10:36.102
Unnecessary?!

10:36.104 --> 10:37.906
Everyone's worried about you, you know!

10:38.756 --> 10:41.252
I heard you were
in another fight yesterday.

10:41.464 --> 10:43.483
You're really something.

10:43.485 --> 10:45.424
No wonder you got a fever.

10:45.426 --> 10:48.333
...It's not because of the fight.

10:50.683 --> 10:52.293
Were you stressing over

10:52.295 --> 10:55.617
how you were freezing up
because you started liking your friends?

10:56.515 --> 10:57.693
Here, some water!

10:58.505 --> 10:59.886
Who the hell told you?!

10:59.888 --> 11:01.984
You're so easy to read.

11:01.986 --> 11:03.943
Ume told me.

11:08.408 --> 11:10.074
I just don't buy it!

11:10.796 --> 11:14.802
Like hell something soft and fuzzy
like that would make me freeze up.

11:16.548 --> 11:20.264
But you really did freeze up, didn't you?

11:23.283 --> 11:27.358
Whatever the reason,
there's no changing what happened.

11:27.360 --> 11:29.427
Why not find a workaround instead?

11:29.429 --> 11:30.786
A workaround?

11:31.066 --> 11:34.322
Like relying on those around you
who can move.

11:36.298 --> 11:37.786
Y-You're kidding.

11:37.788 --> 11:38.893
I can handle it myself.

11:39.645 --> 11:42.021
This is my problem.

11:45.940 --> 11:46.020
(HMPH)

11:46.020 --> 11:47.040
Hey, I was still eatin'!
(HMPH)

11:47.040 --> 11:47.950
Hey, I was still eatin'!

11:48.409 --> 11:51.023
Can you even make something like this
by yourself?

11:52.091 --> 11:52.904
What?

11:53.227 --> 11:56.309
All you have to do
is throw ingredients into the heat,

11:56.311 --> 11:58.667
but you don't even have a stove,
a pot, or ingredients.

11:58.669 --> 12:00.153
Wh-What are you...

12:00.155 --> 12:04.418
Nire and the others brought those
while you were sleeping.

12:04.692 --> 12:06.924
And I made this for you.

12:07.349 --> 12:09.562
It's because of someone else

12:09.563 --> 12:12.999
that you could rest
and wake up with food and water.

12:13.307 --> 12:16.240
I-It's not like I can't buy my own food.

12:16.242 --> 12:18.852
That's not what I'm getting at.

12:19.369 --> 12:21.899
Even if you could've done it on your own,

12:21.901 --> 12:26.217
since someone else did it for you,
you were able to focus on something else.

12:26.514 --> 12:32.236
People can only do so much
with their limited time.

12:33.365 --> 12:35.290
There isn't a lot I can do.

12:41.463 --> 12:43.078
Well, I say that, but...

12:43.457 --> 12:46.278
Letting other people do things for you
and relying on them

12:47.266 --> 12:50.328
can be a bit scary at first.

13:08.532 --> 13:09.532
Alright.

13:11.097 --> 13:12.490
Hey, Kaji.

13:12.492 --> 13:13.712
You've got a guest.

13:20.978 --> 13:22.344
Oh, it's you.

13:23.497 --> 13:26.168
I... wanna talk with you for a bit.

13:27.827 --> 13:30.374
With me? About what?

13:30.817 --> 13:32.392
About that last fight...

13:34.701 --> 13:36.892
What's this?
So your "guest" was a first-year?

13:36.894 --> 13:38.405
Well, look at you!

13:38.407 --> 13:40.139
You're a full-fledged senpai now!

13:40.405 --> 13:41.977
Shut up, you guys!

13:41.979 --> 13:43.433
That hair...

13:43.435 --> 13:45.317
So you're Sakura.

13:45.319 --> 13:46.211
You sure put up—

13:46.213 --> 13:47.982
You mean the first-year
who beat Shishitoren?

13:47.984 --> 13:49.107
Amazing!

13:49.111 --> 13:51.552
You even tamed a guy like that?

13:51.554 --> 13:51.620
-Shaddap!
-Tamed...?

13:51.620 --> 13:52.934
(Tamed…)
-Shaddap!
-Tamed...?

13:52.934 --> 13:53.481
(Tamed…)

13:53.481 --> 13:54.574
Let's go somewhere else.
(Tamed…)

13:55.011 --> 13:56.212
Kusumi! Enomoto!

13:56.214 --> 13:56.993
Yeah?

13:56.997 --> 13:59.746
Don't let these guys follow us
no matter what!

13:59.748 --> 14:00.747
Roger.

14:00.749 --> 14:01.638
Let's go.

14:01.640 --> 14:02.830
Listen herrre!

14:02.832 --> 14:05.304
Get back to yerrr seats!

14:07.642 --> 14:09.845
So? What did you wanna talk about?

14:10.663 --> 14:13.049
When we were fighting with KEEL...

14:13.580 --> 14:14.621
I...

14:14.949 --> 14:17.740
thought I could handle it on my own.

14:18.971 --> 14:20.949
But that wasn't the case at all.

14:23.095 --> 14:25.852
In the end, we needed you guys
to clean up our mess.

14:27.218 --> 14:29.862
There wasn't much I could do.

14:30.930 --> 14:35.808
That's why I get that I gotta rely
on others and let them help me,

14:37.554 --> 14:38.554
but...

14:39.549 --> 14:40.549
But what?

14:41.110 --> 14:43.742
You leave everything
to your vice captains.

14:44.145 --> 14:45.282
Like earlier,

14:45.284 --> 14:46.296
and fighting,

14:46.298 --> 14:47.515
and when you go on patrol.

14:49.549 --> 14:51.502
How can you let them handle so much?

14:52.830 --> 14:56.124
How? How do I be like that?

15:02.559 --> 15:03.391
Say somethin—

15:03.393 --> 15:04.575
Shut up for a sec.

15:09.668 --> 15:11.649
H-Hey!

15:27.256 --> 15:29.599
Hey, where are you goin'?!

15:32.767 --> 15:34.568
Th-The roof?

15:34.898 --> 15:39.044
I heard that this kind of talk is best
done somewhere high and spacious.

15:41.430 --> 15:45.634
So, why am I able
to rely on others, was it?

15:46.883 --> 15:48.875
Because I can't do everything on my own.

15:50.190 --> 15:52.902
B-But saying somethin' like that

15:53.214 --> 15:55.899
is like admittin' you're weak!

15:56.479 --> 15:58.025
I can't do something like that...

15:58.850 --> 15:59.159
(GLANCE)

15:59.159 --> 16:00.599
Wh-What?
(GLANCE)

16:00.599 --> 16:00.600
(GLANCE)

16:07.860 --> 16:08.258
(Green Tea)

16:08.258 --> 16:09.610
You know what this is?
(Green Tea)

16:09.610 --> 16:09.621
You know what this is?

16:10.756 --> 16:12.598
Tea, I mean, green tea?

16:12.600 --> 16:13.750
Right, but it's coffee inside.

16:13.750 --> 16:15.500
(SMUG)
Right, but it's coffee inside.

16:15.502 --> 16:16.040
Hah? What the hell—
(SMUG)

16:16.040 --> 16:17.230
Hah? What the hell—

16:17.232 --> 16:21.426
No matter how much I call this green tea,
the inside is still coffee.

16:22.421 --> 16:25.716
Just because the label's changed
doesn't mean the contents have.

16:26.064 --> 16:27.891
No shit.

16:27.893 --> 16:30.930
Then isn't pretending you can do something
when you can't,

16:30.930 --> 16:31.590
(Green Tea)
Then isn't pretending you can do something
when you can't,

16:31.591 --> 16:36.310
the same as calling coffee green tea and
trying to pass it off as the real thing?
(Green Tea)

16:36.310 --> 16:36.788
the same as calling coffee green tea and
trying to pass it off as the real thing?

16:37.353 --> 16:40.576
You know you can't do much on your own.

16:41.213 --> 16:43.511
You know you need to rely on others.

16:43.848 --> 16:45.373
But you still can't do it.

16:46.653 --> 16:48.296
Because you're scared.

16:48.748 --> 16:50.793
Scared of being rejected by others.

16:53.208 --> 16:54.868
That...

16:54.870 --> 16:56.015
can't be...

16:56.695 --> 16:58.436
I was supposed to have given up already.

16:58.881 --> 17:01.018
Rejection, denial, being turned down...

17:01.316 --> 17:03.929
I told myself I didn't care
what people thought of me.

17:04.574 --> 17:05.694
I didn't care...

17:07.569 --> 17:10.735
I wasn't supposed to care.

17:12.480 --> 17:18.305
They saw what I could do from how I fought
and decided to make me grade captain.

17:19.355 --> 17:20.358
Nirei,

17:20.360 --> 17:21.361
Suo,

17:22.067 --> 17:23.871
Tsugeura, Kiryu,

17:24.342 --> 17:25.392
and everyone else...

17:26.598 --> 17:28.114
But I...

17:28.604 --> 17:31.218
I couldn't live up to their expectations.

17:32.851 --> 17:35.611
If I admit that in front of them,

17:36.254 --> 17:38.996
and even begin leaning on them...

17:46.261 --> 17:50.852
I don't know how you think people see you,

17:51.432 --> 17:56.355
but everyone already knows
you're scared shitless.

17:59.701 --> 18:00.995
H-How did...

18:00.997 --> 18:03.564
p-p-people know about that?!

18:03.813 --> 18:05.522
Who wouldn't?

18:05.527 --> 18:07.786
Especially if you snap like that.

18:09.517 --> 18:11.204
Well, uh...

18:11.804 --> 18:12.230
You know how cats and dogs snap at you
when they're scared?

18:12.230 --> 18:15.751
(MROOOOOOOOOOWR)
You know how cats and dogs snap at you
when they're scared?

18:15.753 --> 18:16.542
It's kinda like that.
(MROOOOOOOOOOWR)

18:16.544 --> 18:18.248
Cats and dogs...?
(MROOOOOOOOOOWR)

18:18.248 --> 18:18.250
(MROOOOOOOOOOWR)

18:21.209 --> 18:24.309
I heard ghosts show up here on the roof.

18:28.271 --> 18:30.574
Someone who sneaked up here
at night said it.

18:31.286 --> 18:34.421
That there was a woman
in a one-piece dress standing there.

18:35.429 --> 18:38.170
But when they checked it out
the next day...

18:39.505 --> 18:42.727
It was just a plastic bag wrapped
around a shovel.

18:44.196 --> 18:48.522
He just assumed it was a ghost
and got freaked out for no reason.

18:48.524 --> 18:49.524
Right.

18:50.198 --> 18:54.802
You assumed you'd be rejected
and got freaked out for no reason.

18:55.344 --> 18:58.949
There's no way you can figure out
what someone else is thinking.

18:59.976 --> 19:01.879
But even so, your friends,

19:02.190 --> 19:04.838
when they saw the version of you
that you think is weak,

19:05.238 --> 19:08.091
even when they saw you snap and freak out,

19:08.390 --> 19:12.098
not a single one of them rejected you.

19:13.629 --> 19:17.594
They're not looking at what you can do.

19:17.596 --> 19:20.063
They're looking at you.

19:22.278 --> 19:28.113
Despite that, you keep getting scared
of rejection even when it's not happening.

19:28.901 --> 19:30.206
From my perspective,

19:30.208 --> 19:35.532
you're the one who's not seeing them
for who they are.

19:36.594 --> 19:39.526
I don't know what happened to you
that made you this way.

19:39.942 --> 19:43.230
But I get how it feels.

19:44.091 --> 19:45.992
That's why I'm telling you this.

19:46.360 --> 19:47.304
Sakura-san!

19:47.306 --> 19:48.298
Sakura-kun!

19:48.300 --> 19:49.264
Sakura-kun!

19:49.266 --> 19:50.460
Sakura-chan!

19:51.491 --> 19:53.241
Trust in what you see.

19:53.684 --> 19:55.426
Believe in them.

19:59.170 --> 20:01.198
Tch, I've said too much.

20:04.445 --> 20:06.269
You nailed it, Kaji!

20:06.271 --> 20:07.446
Hey, stop it already.

20:07.448 --> 20:09.965
You've both grown so much!

20:12.542 --> 20:16.194
Sorry, we didn't mean to eavesdrop.

20:16.240 --> 20:17.451
(GAH!)

20:17.451 --> 20:18.210
I have to say, Kaji!
(GAH!)

20:18.210 --> 20:19.339
I have to say, Kaji!

20:19.341 --> 20:21.830
You're starting to sound
a lot like Hiragi!

20:21.830 --> 20:21.848
(GYA?!)
You're starting to sound
a lot like Hiragi!

20:21.848 --> 20:22.570
(GYA?!)

20:23.963 --> 20:25.094
By the way, about your talk—

20:36.581 --> 20:38.506
This one's on you, Umemiya.

20:43.794 --> 20:47.682
Man, Kaji's really grown.

20:47.684 --> 20:48.969
That was a great punch.

20:48.971 --> 20:50.790
He should've kicked you too.

20:52.059 --> 20:53.453
So, Sakura,

20:53.693 --> 20:55.934
what are your thoughts
after listening to Kaji?

20:55.936 --> 20:57.906
M-My thoughts?

20:58.500 --> 21:00.852
There's plenty of stuff I can't do.

21:01.306 --> 21:04.000
I mess up and look lame
a lot of times too.

21:04.928 --> 21:06.870
But I'm not scared.

21:06.870 --> 21:06.881
(BOFURIN)
But I'm not scared.

21:06.881 --> 21:07.203
(BOFURIN)

21:07.203 --> 21:13.941
That's because I know that everyone here
will accept me no matter what.
(BOFURIN)

21:13.941 --> 21:14.130
(BOFURIN)

21:14.436 --> 21:15.764
So I figure,

21:16.071 --> 21:19.008
if someone else can't do something,
I'll just do it for them.

21:19.317 --> 21:22.517
Even if they mess up and look lame...
I'll still like them.

21:23.031 --> 21:25.148
That's how it is for everyone.

21:25.373 --> 21:27.480
We rely on each other,

21:27.482 --> 21:30.095
forgive and are forgiven,
and stay together.

21:31.669 --> 21:33.002
That's why it's okay.

21:33.607 --> 21:34.922
Believe in Kaji.

21:35.448 --> 21:37.036
Believe in your friends.

21:37.869 --> 21:40.361
And jump in there with all you've got!

21:45.260 --> 21:48.295
And you can't even look him in the eye?

21:49.617 --> 21:51.305
I'm one to talk...

21:51.925 --> 21:54.671
So look us in the eye too.

22:02.991 --> 22:07.461
Still, to think Kaji
would give advice to a kouhai!

22:08.870 --> 22:10.942
Isn't that nice, Senpai?

22:13.250 --> 22:14.351
Yeah.

22:18.492 --> 22:20.939
C'mon, sit down.

22:22.257 --> 22:24.667
Why are we on the roof?

22:25.198 --> 22:26.998
Why?

22:27.756 --> 22:32.458
'Cause this kind of talk is best done
somewhere high and spacious.

22:35.007 --> 22:38.014
(Senpai's Teachings)

23:30.311 --> 23:33.439
Wow, I got to see something great today!

23:33.441 --> 23:36.261
It would've been even better
if ya didn't show up.

23:36.263 --> 23:38.262
Alright, today's worth celebrating!

23:38.264 --> 23:39.852
Let's call everyone and throw a party!

23:39.854 --> 23:41.851
Alright,
time to do a schoolwide broadcast—

23:41.853 --> 23:42.952
Stop it!

23:42.954 --> 23:45.558
What're ya gonna do
if everyone hears about their talk?!

23:45.560 --> 23:50.002
Ehhh? Everyone should hear about
how Kaji and Sakura have grown!

23:50.004 --> 23:54.039
Just try it. Kaji's sugar intake's
gonna shoot through the roof.

23:54.041 --> 23:56.492
Why? It's not something
to be ashamed about.

23:56.687 --> 23:59.333
Man, I'm so happy!
